PHOTO-008 (sharpen, blur and noise tools) is implemented on branch
feat/PHOTO-008-sharpen-blur-noise — check `gh pr list` before assuming it's
merged.

What it added, and the two things worth knowing before touching this area:
- spatialPass.ts is the first neighbourhood pass in the photo pipeline
  (toneLUT, channelLUT, levelsCurves and colorPass are all per-pixel or
  per-channel maps). The gaussian is three box passes per axis, which is
  O(1) per pixel in the radius; a textbook kernel was far too slow to redo
  per animation frame.
- Every spatial radius is a *fraction of the render's shorter edge*, never a
  pixel count. That is load-bearing: renderAdjustedImage is called at three
  different sizes for the same image (full-res bake, 1400px preview, 256px
  histogram proxy), and a pixel radius would make them disagree. Grain needed
  its own version of this — grainParticleSize() grows the particle with the
  image, since a particle fixed at one pixel is finer on the bake than on the
  preview it was judged from.
- useAdjustedPreviewCanvas now renders at a 1400px cap (PREVIEW_MAX_EDGE),
  where it previously used the image's natural size. flattenImage (PHOTO-006's
  port-back) still bakes at full resolution and is unaffected.

Known limitation, deliberate: flatten-on-exit on a large uncapped image now
takes 1-4s with the blur/sharpen tools active, where it was near-instant when
the pipeline was LUT-only. It's a one-time operation on exit, not per frame,
and there is no progress indicator. Worth a ticket if it bites.

Next ticket: no auto-pickable one. What's open, each needing a decision:
- PHOTO-009 (geometry tools: crop, straighten, arbitrary rotate, flip,
  resize/resample, perspective) — the natural next in the photo sequence. It
  is a separate raster pipeline from Canvas's existing crop tools (UX-009,
  UX-021), so decide up front whether the two share geometry code or stay
  apart.
- PHOTO-011 (selection and local masking) is foundational and unlocks locally
  scoped versions of the PHOTO-008/010/012 tools, so it is worth sequencing
  before those where possible — including before PHOTO-012's filters.
- PROD-002 (further product families) — explicitly "not yet scoped". Extends
  PROD-001's preset model past circles, so it needs a shape decision first:
  products.ts's ProductShape covers 'circle' and 'rect' only, and
  productGuides.ts draws arcs and rectangles directly. A die-cut sticker or a
  rounded-rect card needs a path-based guide.
- BOOK-001 (page templates system) — large, needs its own phasing pass.
- BOOK-004 (print export modal) — deferred by the user pending a rethink;
  don't resume without them re-raising it.

Two boundaries left by PROD-001, both deliberate:
- Page thumbnails (PageBar/PageStack) draw book guides but not product
  guides, so a pin page's thumbnail is a plain white square.
- Resizing the artboard (UX-014) on a product page leaves the guide circle at
  its original diameter, so the two stop agreeing. Book pages have the same
  gap with their bleed.
